{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1086186-kitsune-and-hengeyokai-auspices-and-hengeyokai-stuff","id":1086186,"title":"Kitsune and Hengeyokai Auspices and Hengeyokai stuff","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-01T07:26:45-07:00","id":1086186,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Kitsune and Hengeyokai Auspices and Hengeyokai stuff","content":"So it was really illuminating when W20 Changing Breeds cleared up that Hengeyokai Auspices are added to a shifters Auspice rather then replacing one.<br /> <br /> But the Original Hengeyokai book kind of sneaks in at the end of their Section on Kitsune Paths (their version of Auspices) that a Jade bowl appears to represent the Hengeyokai. The implication being you can choose this bowl to join the Beast Courts rather then choose a Path.<br /> <br /> So does that mean the Kitsune who join the Beast Courts don't have a Path and only an Auspice Role like Mirror or Pillar? If so I would improve the Auspice to have gift costs of primary auspice rather then that secondary auspice x4 cost.<br /> <br /> Or do you think a Kitsune still chooses a Bowl but can choose the Jade Bowl as a 2nd one.<br /> <br /> <br /> And another thing some Hengeyokai can just keep their native Renown system but still work for the Courts. So does Court Auspices apply if you actually use the Hengeyokai Renown systems? Doing so after all means for a lot of folks doing that whole Renown Reset Rebirth rite.<br /> <br /> And how do you think it would be treated having different Shifters pair up romantically. After all you don't get metis that way. I was thinking something along the Line of a Metis Hakken seeking love from say a Kitsune?<br /> <br /> The Zhong Lung Being Mokole used to interbreed with other Shifters and their kin in ancient times.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T07:52:07-07:00","id":1086194,"title":"","content":"Wasn't it a silver bowl, and far less certainty with what, exactly, it meant, but with heavy hints that it was a cause of pain in one NPC's life?<br /> <br /> Also, W20 CB detailed particularly bad things being afoot when Kitsune bed down with other changers, since it results in a rather significant chance of killing said bedmates or spouses. Even if you're not getting kids, it might get frowned upon for that very reason, unless the metis is a discreet lover on the side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T08:02:08-07:00","id":1086201,"title":"","content":"I yes thank you, I forgot their curse extended even to things like sterile metis. I figure it would be a tragedy anyways, I mean metis scream unhappy endings.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T13:04:00-07:00","id":1086302,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that the silver bowl was unique to that one particular NPC and the vast majority of Kitsune choose from one of the 4 standard element bowls (Clay, Lighting, Mist and Lava).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T14:44:41-07:00","id":1086340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1086186-kitsune-and-hengeyokai-auspices-and-hengeyokai-stuff#post1086186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how do you think it would be treated having different Shifters pair up romantically. After all you don't get metis that way. I was thinking something along the Line of a Metis Hakken seeking love from say a Kitsune?</div> </div> </div> </div>It used to be that this fell under the &quot;Being honorably mated&quot; area of Renown. Being in a relationship that is unlikely to produce a new member of your whatever you are is socially frowned upon. This may be an even bigger deal in the Beast Courts, where concepts of &quot;face&quot; and social shame/ostracism are a more significant part of the culture. However, it may also be perfectly acceptable to have some sort of &quot;public&quot; relationship with a spouse and children that is more businesslike in nature while also maintaining a private relationship with someone else. Personally, I'd expect that as long as any shifter who is able to reproduce is making a public effort to do so, others are unlikely to care much about whatever else they are doing romantically or sexually. Metis may be a special case, however, as they are so tied up in their culture's concepts of sexual taboo/sin that others may take offense at their engaging in any sort of romantic or sexual activity. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T14:45:40-07:00","id":1086341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1086186-kitsune-and-hengeyokai-auspices-and-hengeyokai-stuff?p=1086302#post1086302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that the silver bowl was unique to that one particular NPC and the vast majority of Kitsune choose from one of the 4 standard element bowls (Clay, Lighting, Mist and Lava).</div> </div> </div> </div>At the end of the focus new character's story section, she sees the silver bowl at her feet and reaches for it, just as her father did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T14:53:29-07:00","id":1086344,"title":"","content":"So is it standard that Kitsune see 5 bowls, one of which is silver, or is it not standard and this character and her father were just special?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T15:25:23-07:00","id":1086358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1086186-kitsune-and-hengeyokai-auspices-and-hengeyokai-stuff?p=1086344#post1086344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is it standard that Kitsune see 5 bowls, one of which is silver, or is it not standard and this character and her father were just special?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably the latter, but I never really thought to ask about it to any official channels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T21:42:52-07:00","id":1086464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1086186-kitsune-and-hengeyokai-auspices-and-hengeyokai-stuff?p=1086344#post1086344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is it standard that Kitsune see 5 bowls, one of which is silver, or is it not standard and this character and her father were just special?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I got the idea that the Kitsune &quot;fifth auspice&quot; was meant to be a plot hook.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T22:12:13-07:00","id":1086473,"title":"","content":"So I'm the only one here who got the impression that the Fifth bowl was supposed to represent the Beast Courts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T08:32:46-07:00","id":1086651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1086186-kitsune-and-hengeyokai-auspices-and-hengeyokai-stuff?p=1086473#post1086473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm the only one here who got the impression that the Fifth bowl was supposed to represent the Beast Courts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's really ambiguous. We don't have much to go on, and the options are wide open..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T03:57:31-07:00","id":1087085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1086186-kitsune-and-hengeyokai-auspices-and-hengeyokai-stuff#post1086186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or do you think a Kitsune still chooses a Bowl but can choose the Jade Bowl as a 2nd one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The acceptance into the Beast Court &amp; the Kitsune &quot;baptising&quot; are governed by tow distinct Rites with unchangeable effect. Kitsunes have their Paths &amp; also choose a Pillar. The &quot;fifth bowl&quot; is just a trap for the too confidents &amp; self-centered. Pride is a great flaw of the Kitsune, I'd use the fifth path as a safety pressure valve . You grab it, become self-important, choosen-cursed and you able to grab an other one. (And buy some appropiate Merits &amp; Flaws.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1086186-kitsune-and-hengeyokai-auspices-and-hengeyokai-stuff#post1086186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And another thing some Hengeyokai can just keep their native Renown system but still work for the Courts. So does Court Auspices apply if you actually use the Hengeyokai Renown systems? Doing so after all means for a lot of folks doing that whole Renown Reset Rebirth rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my interpretation, you only receive the benefits of Pillars &amp; Court membership, if you'd follow the Hengeyokai Renown system. But I'm harsh. If you can interpret a certain rule in two different way, I always choose which is less benefical to the players. This is the World of Darkness &amp; not the world of cheesmakers!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1086186-kitsune-and-hengeyokai-auspices-and-hengeyokai-stuff#post1086186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how do you think it would be treated having different Shifters pair up romantically. After all you don't get metis that way. I was thinking something along the Line of a Metis Hakken seeking love from say a Kitsune?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm avid Kitsune-player, and I always wanted to have sex with pretty everything, except other changers and vampires. (They are cold to the touch.) The rate of death during the birth is extreamly high, the gain - a mixed breed, diluted blooded kin - is low. Of course you coud use condoms, but I'd give some negative Renown for it.<br /> Maybe Karin Jarlsdottir would change my mind...<br /> <br /> To have some hup\u00e1k with a Metis would be an another matter. The Curse doesn't affect Metis at all. Or any sexual affair without a pregnancy ending in a births. Metis are sterile, so their relationship would be safe -from this perspective-, but I would not think that Gaia &amp; da spirits would see it honorable. Proliferating is a strong need, a Sacred Duty. Doig the deed with a metis could be fun, but a waste of time.<br /> <br /> About social shame/ostracism: a Kitsune in the public would not shame themeshelves in the face of their peers or make their &quot;friends&quot; embarassed / discomforted. In ther beds they would not give a ****. Or they would give. Whatever.<br /> <br /> Also the different worldviews of the B\u00e9te would make the relationship extreamly messy &amp; the Rage can make a kitchen-fight a bloody mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","user":"Lachdanan","date":". 05-04-2017, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T06:25:35-07:00","id":1087130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1086186-kitsune-and-hengeyokai-auspices-and-hengeyokai-stuff?p=1087085#post1087085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm avid Kitsune-palyer, and I always wanted to have sex with pretty everything, except other changers and vampires. (They are cold to the touch.) The rate of death during the birth is extreamly high, the gain - a mixed breed, diluted blooded kin - is low. Of course you colud use condoms, but I'd give some negative Renown for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's difficult for your Trueborn Child to assassinate your seduction victims for you if you use condoms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T06:32:11-07:00","id":1110817,"title":"","content":"Ehem... While <i>Metis</i> are sterile, <i>Shinju</i> are not. And neither is producing a <i>Shinju</i> a stain on a Kitsune's vest. No, Kitsune are plainly better off... at least in this little area.<br /> <br /> <br /> But as we are at it... How to interpret &quot;Kitsune rely heavily upon their magical strength and versatility. Not only are they able to learn potent Gifts of their own, but can easily learn the Gifts of other Changing Breeds as well, as long as they have a teacher for the Gift. The experience cost is the same as for a non-breed/auspice/tribal Gift.&quot; stated on <i>W20 CB</i> p.126?<br /> <br /> Do Kitsune gain more choice what to learn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T07:27:54-07:00","id":1110841,"title":"","content":"Yes, they can learn any Gift or Rite, from any species of Fera (CB, .p. 126), and they can learn the Paths and Rituals of mortal magicians (CB, p. 208). With their exceptional longevity, a Rank 5 Kitsune could learn every possible Gift and Rite (and round it out with every possible mortal Path and Ritual).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T13:29:45-07:00","id":1110975,"title":"","content":"For gifts the limit up to level 3 for other feras gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T15:24:23-07:00","id":1111034,"title":"","content":"Kitsune can learn <i>all </i>the Fera Gifts as long as they possess a high enough Rank (if you read their write up in CB 20, they have no Rank restrictions, unlike the members of the Hengeyokai in the previous edition).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 07-03-2017, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T15:23:47-07:00","id":1111835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1086186-kitsune-and-hengeyokai-auspices-and-hengeyokai-stuff?p=1111034#post1111034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kitsune can learn <i>all </i>the Fera Gifts as long as they possess a high enough Rank (if you read their write up in CB 20, they have no Rank restrictions, unlike the members of the Hengeyokai in the previous edition).</div> </div> </div> </div>At least on the page you quoting (CB, p126), it doesn't say anything about &quot;all&quot; Gifts. It says:&quot; <span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Not only are they able to learn potent </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Gifts of their own, but can easily learn the Gifts of other </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Changing Breeds as well, as long as they have a teacher </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">for the Gift.&quot;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> So while you can decide that they are an exception to the general rule of Rank 3 limits, the book does not specifically say they are.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would limit them to Rank 3 and below. The higher Rank Gifts are just too aptitude specific in general imo. Besides that, I don't think I agree that 1600 years is enough to lean every Changing Breed Gift (even just up to Rank 3) plus all Rites plus all Hedge Magic. If that were the case, then the Kitsune would be a hell of a lot more powerful than they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 07-05-2017, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T15:25:46-07:00","id":1111838,"title":"","content":"There is no such limit in CB20. At least that I could find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T05:00:38-07:00","id":1113685,"title":"","content":"The Problem I have is: It does seem to imply or express some rule change, but it doesn't say WHAT it does change exactly. Lift some limit? Allow learning from any suitable teacher? I couldn't even find the &quot;rank 3 limit&quot; in either CB20 or W20 - nor real explicit rules for cross-learnign gifts actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T07:04:57-07:00","id":1113717,"title":"","content":"Well, the Kitsune section specifically mentions that they have to learn such Gifts from a teacher with the Gift in question (though that does mean that they could potentially learn the three Ratkin Form Gifts if they could find a willing teacher, which would be amusing). With their longevity, Kitsune potentialy become the repository of every Gift known to the members of the Hengeyokai. The Kitsune might even have preserved Gifts lost by the other Fera, like the Gifts of the Bunyip or the Okane, though they would probably be reluctant to share them with just anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}